          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="KComboBox" name="encodingSelector">
            <property name="toolTip">
             <string>The character set to use to decode the strings sent by the core.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="whatsThis">
             <string>&lt;p&gt;Although MLDonkey does not understand about character encodings, you may well encounter text on the Donkey network that has been encoded in various national character sets. While you should, in general, use the ISO 8859-1 encoding - the de-facto network standard - you can choose a different character encoding here if you expect most of the text you encounter to be encoded in a certain national character set.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Note:&lt;/b&gt; Changing this causes KMLDonkey to reconnect to the core. Changing it to something incompatible with the ISO 8859-1 character set &lt;em&gt;may&lt;/em&gt; cause unpredictable behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
         </layout>
        </item>
